# Valid draft v0.1 coverage example; one diagram.
object "Order".
object "Priority Order" informatical systemic.
object "Order 001" informatical systemic.
object "Order Record" informatical environmental.
object "Operator" physical environmental.
object "Machine" physical systemic.
object "Machine Component" physical systemic.
object "Receipt" informatical systemic.

process "Order Handling" informatical systemic.
process "Priority Handling" informatical systemic.
process "Handling Run 001" informatical environmental.
process "Printing" physical systemic.

"Order" has state "pending".
"Order" has state "approved".
"Order" has state "completed".

# Aggregation: object/object and process/process.
"Machine" consists of "Machine Component".
"Order Handling" consists of "Printing".

# Exhibition: all four allowed type combinations.
"Order" exhibits "Order Record".
"Machine" exhibits "Printing".
"Order Handling" exhibits "Order Record".
"Order Handling" exhibits "Priority Handling".

# Specialization and instantiation for each entity type.
"Priority Order" is an "Order".
"Priority Handling" is "Order Handling".
"Order 001" is an instance of "Order".
"Handling Run 001" is an instance of "Order Handling".

# Tagged links: both directions and both allowed type combinations.
"Order" relates to "Receipt" as "documented by".
"Order Handling" relates to "Printing" as "scheduled before".
"Order" relates bidirectionally to "Order Record" as "corresponds to".
"Printing" relates bidirectionally to "Delivery" as "coordinates with".

# Procedural links: all five kinds.
"Printing" consumes "Order Record".
"Printing" yields "Receipt".
"Order Handling" affects "Order".
"Operator" handles "Order Handling".
"Printing" requires "Machine".

# Forward reference above; physical/environmental process styling.
process "Delivery" physical environmental.
